# Cloudflare Pages redirects — path-based, same-host only.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file can only redirect paths on whatever host serves
# the Pages project. It CANNOT fix the old site's http:// vs https://
# or www vs bare-domain inconsistency (the old WordPress site
# self-referenced http://www.strichnet.com throughout its feed and
# sitemap). That canonicalization has to happen one level up, in
# Cloudflare's dashboard for the strichnet.com zone:
#
#   1. SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates -> "Always Use HTTPS": on
#   2. Rules -> Redirect Rules -> create a rule:
#        When incoming hostname equals "www.strichnet.com"
#        Then redirect to https://strichnet.com/${uri.path} (301, preserve query string)
#
# Once both are set, every historical http://www.strichnet.com/x link
# lands on https://strichnet.com/x, and everything below only has to
# handle path-level differences.

# The old RSS feed lived at /feed/. Astro's RSS integration serves
# /rss.xml instead (see src/pages/rss.xml.js) — feed readers follow
# redirects transparently, so nobody subscribed since 2017 gets dropped.
/feed/  /rss.xml  301

