# Per-post redirects.
#
# Posts used to serve at the site root (/post-name/) to match the old
# WordPress permalinks exactly. The Myscholar-style rebuild moved them to
# /blog/<slug>, which is what makes the blog index, tag pages and
# breadcrumbs coherent — so every one of those 17 root permalinks now
# needs a 301. Twelve years of inbound links point at them.
#
# Each line below is generated from a post's `originalPath` frontmatter.
# scripts/check-redirects.mjs asserts that every published post's
# originalPath appears here and fails `npm run build` if one is missing,
# so adding a post with a legacy URL can't silently break it.
#
# Do NOT collapse these into a splat like `/* /blog/:splat`. That would
# also swallow /handbook/*, /projects/*, /uses and /now.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
